│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses a highly parameter-efficien
│                          │ across all wires for each rotation layer. While thi
│                          │ smooth loss landscape, it limits the model's expres
│                          │ records via `IsingZZ` on specific qubit pairs with 
│                          │ needs the ability to break symmetry.               
│                          │                                                    
│                          │ By making the `RY_in` parameters independent for ea
│                          │ "weight" each qubit differently right after the fea
│                          │ making the `RY_out` parameters independent allows t
│                          │ predictive qubits with the Z-axis for the final mea
│                          │ average of all Z expectations). We retain the colle
│                          │ `RX_out` layers to provide regularization. This cha
│                          │ per block from 4 to 18 (110 parameters total) which
│                          │ overfitting but expressive enough to boost training
